{"commit": "0139255a78ada92277ce0d1025c009254ea5b298", "id": "0139255a78ada92277ce0d1025c009254ea5b298-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/georust/rstar", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T002528Z-35710f73", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/0139255a78ada92277ce0d1025c009254ea5b298-1/20260924T002528Z-35710f73/origin.json": "e83d11bef13106a18e2f04ffb3b321935fd396a91e57307dffa05ac37cb82fd9", "evidence/0139255a78ada92277ce0d1025c009254ea5b298-1/20260924T002528Z-35710f73/proposal.json": "d60a2b3510d511d5857bbc503e4a2d973e4a87cf2d7ed6380123c52f74333c33"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "rstar", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Defend against numerical instability when computing number of clusters (#166)", "summary": "OMT bulk loading recursively partitions the input into `number_of_clusters_on_axis` clusters per dimension. For specific input sizes (e.g. `N = MAX_SIZE^k`), the depth calculation `(N as f32).log(MAX_SIZE)` returns `k + eps` instead of `k` exactly; ceil pushes depth one too far, the per-cluster count rounds down to 1, and the recursion never terminates \u2014 eventually overflowing the stack.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:25:28.104140+00:00"}
